## #02 - authoritative workflow homes
For an N5NN source, render the full review under Review - Codex Prime inside that
page's explicit 05.NN.md. Supporting typed records/raw evidence may be stored below
the page but cannot replace the readable review there. Model judgment supplies
outcome, facts/claims, findings, limits, questions, Director replies and next action.
Compute supplies headings, ordering, required fields, source/hash links and layout.
Do not invent missing judgment, acceptance, release, closure or source evidence.
Preserve original wording, including dissent and Director replies. Every meaningful
input field must be rendered or explicitly referenced in the durable typed record;
reject unknown fields rather than silently losing them.
N7NN has its own 06.NN.review.md with 05.NN.pack.md and 05.NN.return.md. Declare this
separate route without assigning it an N1NN address. The first implementation must
at minimum support the N5NN path and refuse unsupported source kinds explicitly.
Supporting N7NN rendering is allowed only through this existing rule, not a new one.

## #03 - safe bounded write
Preview is default; apply only to a declared disposable fixture root. Construct no
files in the live work book or app. Validate source page/pass and the intended
Review section. Duplicate/missing headings are refusals, not guessed placements.
Preserve every byte outside the review section and preserve unchanged source text.
Expect the current file hash; refuse stale input. Fill a declared PENDING placeholder
or create a permitted absent review file. Never silently overwrite an existing
substantive review. Exact replay should be idempotent; conflicting judgment must
request an explicit successor process, not erase history. Preserve partial evidence.
Handle Unicode and line endings without silently normalizing unrelated bytes:
support them correctly or refuse an unsupported format without writing.
Document race limitations; compare-then-rename is not proof of race freedom.

## #04 - binding and corrected return-placement seam
The old prime_cycle binds the whole page, so rendering a pointer/review can stale
itself. Demonstrate a lab-level stable binding over explicit task identity, immutable
assignment content, relevant source/evidence identities, exact receipt and agreement.
Rendering a mechanical review must not alter that assignment binding. A real task,
evidence or agreement change must invalidate it. Keep the actual target-file hash
for safe writes distinct from the stable task binding. No production prime_cycle
patch in this pack, and no claim the live cycle has been fixed by this lab.
Use declared exact source/receipt inputs in synthetic fixtures. Verify identities
and label supplied/synthetic evidence honestly. Do not authenticate a receipt from
an arbitrary caller boolean or invent runtime custody. Do not implement reserve,
capture, migration or discovery: consume an explicit return descriptor and document
the adapter required after 0521. The constructor does not allocate destinations.

## #05 - meaningful tests
Demonstrate a full readable review with findings, no-findings, held/incomplete work,
optional/failed checks, minority/dissent and a Director reply. Check missing required
fields, unknown fields, duplicate headings, wrong page/pass, source/receipt mismatch,
stale file hash, conflicting existing review and identical replay. Prove bytes outside
the review region remain exact. Prove rendering preserves task binding but task,
evidence or agreement changes invalidate it. Exercise a new-process reread of the
constructed result. Label synthetic judgments and record actual outputs/exits.
No broad app tests, AR-01 inventory/bridge fixtures, hard-link probes, paid calls,
installations, browser automation or new model sessions.

