### Verified and useful
All ten non-self artifact rows match. Prime independently reran the eight supplied
tests: eight passed, zero skips/errors/failures. Test output was redirected before
execution because the suite's teardown otherwise overwrites builder transcript
and sample files. Original submitted evidence stayed unchanged.
The renderer preserves detailed supplied judgment, dissent and Director replies;
tests cover surrounding bytes, newline handling, ordinary stale hashes and an
explicit lab binding distinct from the target file write token. No production
cycle or app command was changed. Custody is honestly not-established.

### RC-01 - wrong destination page accepted
Independent fixture: page declared 0599.synth-lab/05.01, but target changed to
0588.wrong-page/05.01.md containing the same placeholder. Apply exited 0 and wrote
the full review into that unrelated page. page_rule checks only the basename.
Derive the exact target from the source page/pass and source kind. Compare its
normalized root-relative path, not just the filename. N7NN must similarly remain
on its declared page's 06.NN.review.md. Refuse before creating any support record
or changing a target when the identity/address is inconsistent.

### RC-02 - mismatched return line accepted
Independent fixture: source 0599.synth-lab, but descriptor and typed capture identity
both changed to 0188.unrelated-subject. Apply exited 0. Matching two caller-supplied
strings does not enforce N5NN -> N1NN. Compute the required NN AND subject from the
source, require the descriptor and any typed source origin to match, and preserve
the declared distinction between validated identity and authenticated custody.
Even the suite's ordinary 0199.synthetic-review differs in subject from synth-lab;
the positive fixtures should use internally coherent line identity.

### RC-03 - N is hardcoded to zero and binding lacks source address
The declared N5NN/N7NN interfaces accept only 05NN/07NN under fixed regexes. A
1599 source is refused. Preserve the leading workflow-space digit for matching
return identity and allow the same N7NN page-local rule across supported spaces.
The current binding includes task_id and byte identities but not the source
page/pass. Include explicit normalized origin and the assignment logical identity
so equal task text at a different page is not silently the same bound review.
Mechanical review rendering must still preserve that binding; address, task,
evidence, receipt or agreement changes must change/invalidate it.

